6. Conclusion
Under the joint constraints of the TDMU port axiom system and the MJP-τ critical phase transition conditions, when the full set of boundary conditions (surface light element supply, high-CO₂ atmosphere, liquid ocean, 60–90 °C temperature window, sustained ocean current-tidal pulsations) are satisfied, the system will undergo continuous recursive phase transitions according to this five-step sequence, progressing from surface inorganic components to an organized living system with autonomous internal circulation.

